# Push every commit

Stage explicit paths, never `git add -A` — see `stage-explicit-paths.mdc`.

After any commit, push it:

```bash
git push origin main
```

Do not batch several commits and push later, and do not end a turn with unpushed work.

## Do not watch the deploy

The user does not want deploy monitoring. Do not poll `gh run list`, do not `sleep` waiting for a
workflow, and do not compare deployed asset hashes against the local build. Push and move on.

GitHub Pages serves this project from `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` on push to `main`, so a change
reaches the live site about a minute after the push without anyone watching it.

## When a change "doesn't show up"

Check whether the commit was pushed, then ask which URL the user is on. The dev server and the
deployed site are different things, and Vite moves off port 5173 when that port is already taken.
